learn
Usage: learn [ref CMD | -k WORD | list | progress | reset]

This program. Teaches the vos command surface from nothing to fluent,
in order, and never asks a question it has not already given you the
material to answer.

	learn			resume the curriculum
	learn ref ls		the reference entry for a command
	learn ls		same thing, shorthand
	learn -k pipe		search every entry for a word
	learn list		every documented command
	learn progress		how far along you are
	learn reset		start the curriculum over

Inside a question: ? prints the reference, hint gives a nudge, skip
shows the answer and moves on, quit leaves.

busybox ships no man pages, so these entries are the manual. Every one
is generated from the help text of the binary this image actually
contains, so a flag documented here exists here.

Progress is kept in $XDG_STATE_HOME/learn/progress. On a stick with no
unlocked state partition that lives in RAM and resets at reboot.
